Z||000001||phillip||06-26-2000||11:48 AM||||i think it's the tranny that ends up being further back. i've seen a picture of the rayne eng. one like that. they also make it so the trannys in front, more or less the same drive train turned around. i guess it goes where ths gas tank would and you use a fuel cell. actually i shouldn't have replied to this, i really dont know what i'm talking about. sorry.<P>seriously, if you can find a big fiero parts book ( can't find mine right now or i could be more sure of what i'm saying) or find rayne engineering on the net you can get less mixed up info. ||||reg||1
Z||000002||theogre||06-26-2000||01:34 PM||||not likely.<P>the long mount V8 works only because of the eldorado U turn tranny. That I know of GM doesn't have anything else that will work.<P>The only other tranny I know of that would fit the way you are thinking is a Subaru unit. That one is a short inline tranny with a dif right on the back. It is/was used in Subaru cars in the 70's & early 80's with only front wheel drive. I don't think they use it any more. I think all Subaru are now 4WD. I don't think it would take a V6 HP on it as the clutch was pretty small. (It's basically the same as the 4WD tranny of the time minus the PTO for the rear wheels.)<P>||||reg||1
